# Synthesis of the operand collector with yosys and abc on one library (the distribution's yosys suffices here):
# generic synthesis; the enable and synchronous-reset flops legalised to plain D flops (ASAP7 has no enable flop);
# the logic mapped by abc before the flops so the register names survive; the flops mapped to the library (the
# flop-output inverters this leaves as assignments are instanced by flow/fixnet.py); the area and cell counts by stat.
# usage: flow/synth.sh writes the concrete script from this template.
read_verilog rtl/oc.v
hierarchy -check -top oc
synth -top oc -flatten
dfflegalize -cell $_DFF_P_ 01
@READ_LIBERTY@
abc @LIBERTY_ARGS@
dfflibmap @LIBERTY_ARGS@
opt_clean -purge
tee -o @OUT@.stat.txt stat @LIBERTY_ARGS@
write_verilog -noattr @OUT@.netlist.v
